Data provenance
- Mars 2020 images: all images used by and distributed with MPPP (tests/data/m20/, and the images the
  mask model was trained on) are public products of the NASA Planetary Data System (PDS).
  Credits: Navcam NASA/JPL-Caltech; Mastcam-Z NASA/JPL-Caltech/ASU/MSSS.
- Reconstruction masks, the mask model (mppp_mask_v1, mppp_mask_v2, mppp_mask_v3) and the camera models in
  src/mppp/data/cmods/ (the Navcam cameras and stereo rig, the Hazcam cameras and rigs and the Mastcam-Z focus
  models) are the author's own work.
- The rover model (src/mppp/data/rover/perseverance_rmech.npz, docs/rover/perseverance_rmech.glb) is derived
  from NASA's "Mars Perseverance Rover, 3D Model"
  (https://science.nasa.gov/resource/mars-perseverance-rover-3d-model/). Credit: NASA/JPL-Caltech. It was
  modified by the author (docs/rover-model.md); NASA has not reviewed or endorsed this version.
- The waypoint snapshot (src/mppp/data/M20_waypoints.json) is a copy of the public Mars 2020 rover
  waypoint table.
- The package contains no sensitive or non-public data.

